(d) The permit application shall contain the following:
(1) A narrative describing the proposed wind energy facility, including an overview of the project;
(2) The proposed total rated capacity of the wind energy facility;
(3) The proposed number, representative types and height or range of heights of wind turbines to be constructed; including their generating capacity, dimensions and respective manufacturers, and a description of ancillary facilities;
(4) Identification and location of the properties on which the proposed wind energy facility will be located;
(5) A site plan showing the planned location of all wind turbines, property lines, setback lines, access roads and turnout locations substations, electrical cabling from the wind energy facility to the substations, ancillary equipment, buildings, transmission and distribution lines. The site plan must also include the location of all structures and properties, demonstrating compliance of the setbacks;
(6) A narrative describing how the proposed project will address compliance with any O.C.G.A. § 12-2-8 or any equivalent state statute;
(7) A narrative describing how the proposed project will address compliance with the noise and shadow flicker requirements of this article for the life of the project. The narrative should include a statement that the wind energy facility will be maintained according to the facility manufacturer's recommendations if such recommendations exist. The narrative should also describe how the proposed project will address compliance with O.C.G.A. § 12-2-8 or any equivalent state statute;
(8) Certification by the property owner of compliance with applicable local, state and federal regulations, such as ESA, USCOE, FAA and FCC regulations;
(9) An environmental assessment for class III—IV wind energy facilities, will be provided to the local jurisdiction in order to show that the proposed project meets any relevant federal, state and local requirements;
(10) Other relevant information as may be reasonably requested by the county board of commissioners to ensure compliance with the requirements of this article, such as a topographical survey;
(11) Decommissioning plans that describe the anticipated life of the wind power project, the estimated decommissioning costs in current dollars, the method for ensuring that funds will be available for decommissioning and restoration of site property, and the anticipated manner in which the wind power project will be decommissioned and the site restored;
(12) Signature of the applicant; and
(13) A fee shall be set by the board of commissioners to cover administration of the permitting program.
(e) Throughout the permit process, the applicant shall notify the county department of development services of any proposed changes to the information contained in the permit application that would alter the impact of the project in writing within 120 business days of the change to the plans.
(f) County staff may administratively adopt changes to the approved application that do not materially alter the initial site plan more than ten percent.
(Ord. No. O-120418a, § 25-107, 12-4-2018)
